{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>I [warn] you.</b> When the Sage finished demonstrating that one must guard against the snare of desire, he returned to warn him not to rely on his own wisdom and to despise the commandments of the king of his place because the king is a fool. The expression אני אני אצוך — I warn you, or I caution you, regarding two things: that you not transgress them. The first: what has issued from the mouth of the king. The second: what has issued from your mouth — you too — corresponding to the honored and awesome Name. For an earthly king will not acquit all who transgress his word, and the King of truth will not acquit one who bears His Name in vain."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:19.178997309Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}